Refuse a poll registration once the poll array is full rather than overflow it.

A poll slot is the durable handle evpl_add_poll() hands back, and every
registered poller holds one, so the array must never move or overflow.
evpl_add_poll() now returns NULL when the fixed capacity is reached instead of
writing past it, and the backend pollers that store the handle fail their init
cleanly on the NULL return rather than dereferencing it.

diff --git a/src/core/io_uring/io_uring.c b/src/core/io_uring/io_uring.c
index feae7ea..9179357 100644
--- a/src/core/io_uring/io_uring.c
+++ b/src/core/io_uring/io_uring.c
@@ -359,6 +359,9 @@ evpl_io_uring_create(
 
     ctx->poll = evpl_add_poll(evpl, evpl_io_uring_poll_enter, evpl_io_uring_poll_exit, evpl_io_uring_poll, ctx);
 
+    evpl_io_uring_abort_if(!ctx->poll,
+                           "evpl_add_poll returned NULL: event-loop poll-slot capacity exhausted");
+
     return ctx;
 } /* evpl_io_uring_create */
 
